```mermaid
flowchart LR
  %% Source systems
  subgraph SRC[Source systems]
    S1[S1 - ]
    S2[S2 - ]
    S3[S3 - ]
  end

  %% Ingestion and validation
  subgraph ING[Ingestion]
    MAP[Mappers]
    VAL[Validation gate]
  end

  %% Ontology and store
  subgraph CORE[Ontology and store]
    ONT[Domain model]
    STORE[(Store)]
  end

  %% Agent layer
  subgraph AGENT[Agent layer]
    TPL[Governed templates]
    LOOP[Agent loop]
  end

  %% Human gates
  subgraph GATE[Human gates]
    APPR[Approval queue]
    AUD[Audit log]
  end

  S1 --> MAP
  S2 --> MAP
  S3 --> MAP
  MAP --> VAL
  VAL --> STORE
  ONT --- STORE
  STORE --> TPL
  TPL --> LOOP
  LOOP -->|read| TPL
  LOOP -->|proposed write| APPR
  APPR -->|approved, re-bound| TPL
  LOOP --> AUD
  APPR --> AUD
```

## Conventions

- **Identity order matters.** The minting source appears leftmost among sources and its mapper runs first.
- **The validation gate is always on the path to the store.** A build that has not passed validation is not built.
- **Writes never go store-ward from the agent loop directly.** They route through the approval queue and are re-bound from `{templateId, params}` before executing. Drawing it any other way misrepresents the security model.
- **The audit log receives from every path**, reads included.

